  "explains": "record in src/audit/audit.log.ts logs the time. The class AuditLog is imported by three files: ledger.module.ts (providers), ledger.controller.ts and audit.controller.ts, which take it through their constructors (private readonly audit: AuditLog, private readonly log: AuditLog). In LedgerController the constructor parameter property audit is used by create and remove (this.audit.record), so the routes are POST /api/ledger/entries and DELETE /api/ledger/entries/{id}; list and findOne use only this.ledger and are not reached. The path is the global prefix \"api\" (app.setGlobalPrefix in src/main.ts), the controller path ENTRIES_PATH (\"ledger/entries\", a constant of another file) and the method's path; the route is cited at the method decorator, the controller decorator, the line of ledger.module.ts that lists the controller and the prefix line. AuditController uses AuditLog through this.log in trail, but no module lists the controller, so no route is claimed for it and the run says so (router_unmounted). The client posts to ENTRIES_URL in addEntry and deletes entryUrl(entryId) in removeEntry: two http edges, and the screens /ledger and /ledger/:entryId.",
